erra where does the baby  formula shortage stand right now as of  today we domestically see more product  more baby formula being produced  than we saw several months ago adding to  the supply problem that same abbott  plant had to close because of flooding  which backed up production even more it  reopened july 1st but there are still  delays to store shelves abbott remains  one of only four main companies that  provide about 90 percent of domestic  baby formula in the u.s we also want to  change the policy here  the industry  allowed themselves to be short  and we can't afford that especially with  specialty formula we're going to work to  make sure that they cannot allow  a disruption in a plant that closes down  to disrupt the availability of the  supply that parents need but that future  action would be too late for those like  eight-year-old izzy bradford who we  first met in may she's a third grader  who suffers from a rare disorder known  as pku and relies on a special formula  for about 70 percent of her nutrition  her mom sarah chamberlain says the  hunter formula now  is worse we have less formula than we  did two months ago it's still a scramble  yeah definitely in the last two months i  don't feel like anything has changed i  think we need to recognize this as a  hunger crisis that we have been facing  since february  for cbs mornings i'm meg oliver
 

